  "# ADR-2607180400: BMC loop closes murakumo inference + kotobase dual-write

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-18

## Context

Portfolio BMC ReAct (`70-tools/bmc`) was already driving canvas growth for
cloud-itonami / cloud-murakumo / net-kotobase as *subjects*, but the runtime
was not the three-layer stack:

- think = deterministic `advisor:gate` only (no murakumo LLM)
- persist = git file `canvas-ledger.edn` only (no kotobase)

Owner asked whether the loop was `itonami-defined × murakumo inference ×
kotobase storage`. Answer was no; this ADR lands the missing two edges.

## Decision

1. **Default advisor mode `auto`**: compose `gate-aware-advisor` with
   `llm-advisor` whose `complete` POSTs to
   `https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/chat/completions` (model
   `qwen3.6-35b-a3b`, `chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking=false`). LLM
   failure/empty content → gate-only proposals (fail-soft). `--advisor gate`
   keeps the old path; actor names `advisor:auto` / `advisor:murakumo` /
   `advisor:gate` stamp ledger provenance.

2. **Dual-write after every local ledger append**: git ledger remains SSoT for
   fold/score. Stamped events are projected as entity maps
   (`:db/id \"bmc.event/<seq>\"` + `:bmc.event/*` attrs) and transacted into
   kotobase db `portfolio-bmc-ledger` via
   `70-tools/bmc/bin/kotobase-dual-write.cljs` (kotobase-client CACAO apex
   profile). Identity seed: `70-tools/bmc/.bmc-kotobase-identity.hex`
   (gitignored). Fail-open: remote failure never blocks local append.
   Disable with `--no-kotobase` or `BMC_KOTOBASE_DUAL_WRITE=0`.

3. **Modules**: `gftd.murakumo`, `gftd.kotobase`, CLI `persist-events!` /
   `resolve-advisor` (nbb primary; JVM Bearer path if `KOTOBASE_TOKEN`).

## Consequences

- Live react ticks can use fleet inference and leave an auditable graph on
  kotobase without abandoning git as the portfolio fold SSoT.
- First dual-write mints a new operator DID graph; back up the identity hex.
- Routines (`itonami-react-growth-hourly` / `bmc-business-operate-daily`)
  inherit `auto` + dual-write on next deploy of this superproject path;
  set `BMC_ADVISOR=gate` if a host cannot reach murakumo.
"}]
